testing/fixtures/res — a recorded machine, chosen to break things

WHAT THIS IS

Two complete {proc,sys} roots one sample interval apart:

    testing/fixtures/res/           the first snapshot
    testing/fixtures/res/next/      the second

`kpr_root_set(<dir>/proc, <dir>/sys)` points libkproc at either, which is the
whole of `--fixture`. Every reading in the library is built from that pair, so
a reader that opens /proc/stat directly is a reader this cannot test.

The tree is synthetic rather than copied off a real machine, because a real
machine is a plausible machine: it exercises the common path and none of the
cases below. Each of these is a rule in libkproc that fails silently when it
is wrong, and each shows up here as a wrong number rather than as a crash.

THE TRAPS, AND WHAT EACH ONE CATCHES

  sda1 beside sda            A partition carries a `partition` attribute and
                             its parent does not. Summing every diskstats line
                             counts sda's bytes twice. A regression shows up
                             as an extra row and a doubled rate.

  loop0                      Flagged virtual, not dropped: which devices are
                             interesting is the caller's decision, so the
                             library must report it and mark it.

  eth0 rx_bytes wraps        4294967000 in the first snapshot, 200 in the
                             second — an unsigned 32-bit counter going round.
                             A naive subtraction yields one enormous negative
                             and nothing in the output says so; the reading
                             must be a gap, never a spike.

  pid 800 `backup` in D      Blocked on disk: almost no CPU and real io
                             counters. Sorting on CPU alone hides exactly the
                             process that is holding the machine up.

  pid 300 `sshd` has no io   The file is deliberately absent, which is what
                             EACCES looks like from an unprivileged reader.
                             Both counters must come back KPR_UNREADABLE and
                             render as an em dash. Zero would be a claim that
                             root's sshd has done no disk io.

  conmon 900 -n kdos-apps    pid 950 (firefox-esr) and 951 (Web Content) are
                             its descendants and belong to box `kdos-apps`.
                             pid 700 (foot) has init as its parent and belongs
                             to no box — the boundary, not just the match.

  BAT0 full < full_design    50 Wh of a design 62 Wh. Health is
                             full/full_design = 80.6%, and a battery reporting
                             90% CHARGE is a different fact. A monitor that
                             prints only capacity says nothing about wear.

  card0 i915, card1 amdgpu   amdgpu publishes gpu_busy_percent; i915 does not
                             and never will. The i915 page must report ENGINE
                             TIME from fdinfo (pid 950 fd 7) and must not
                             invent a utilisation percentage. renderD128 is
                             present and must be skipped.

  2 logical / 2 cores / 1 pkg   topology/ is the answer. Counting cpuinfo
                             blocks gives logical CPUs and calling them cores
                             is wrong on every SMT machine.

REGENERATING

There is no generator script: the tree is small, committed, and readable, and
a script would be a second place for the traps to live. Edit the files.

  card0 gt_cur_freq_mhz      MHz, not Hz. The file is named for its unit and a
                             value in the wrong one renders as 1450000000 MHz,
                             which is the shape of every unit bug: a number
                             that is right and a unit that is not.
